# Runtime / GPU Rule

- The current voice launcher intentionally caps LLM GPU layers so ASR, JaiTTS, and RVC can coexist.
- Do not increase LLM offload/context as a "free" optimization without measuring coexistence.
- Distinguish model-file size, VRAM usage, KV/cache usage, and system RAM.
- Prefer explicit runtime profiles over one configuration for every workload.
- Never claim performance numbers that were not measured on the current machine.
- If an optional service is offline, report it honestly and preserve degraded fallback behavior.
